  "rationale": "Methodology and replicate count, re-recorded against the merged tree. Two changes to the instrument, none to the simulation. (1) The standard-error estimator now stratifies on (cellIndex, strategy arm) rather than cellIndex alone. Strategy is a design factor that reaches a run through agentPool instead of factors, so cellIndex never contained it and the estimator folded the whole between-arm spread -- up to 294x on this sweep -- into what it called noise. Measured on the baseline this supersedes, that produced tolerances of 115.2 percent of the metric's own mean on referenceLivingMages and 131.5 percent on referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter: a mechanic could have doubled either and this gate would have reported pass. Taking each of the ten metrics and each of the eight strategies and supposing that arm's contribution fell to zero, 80 of 80 collapses sat inside tolerance. (2) Replicates rise 8 to 16, as a consequence of (1) and not independently: at 8, round-robin over 8 strategies put exactly one run in every (cell, arm) stratum, every within-stratum variance was 0, and the corrected estimator would have produced a tolerance of 0 on every line -- a golden fixture wearing a gate's clothes. Sixteen is the smallest multiple of the pool size that gives each arm a spread of its own. The gate now also carries one line per (metric, arm), because a sweep-level mean over eight strategies that differ by 294x divides any single arm's movement by eight before the gate sees it; per-arm lines compare each strategy against its own committed value at its own noise level. toleranceK is unchanged at 3 and no tolerance was edited by hand. The values below move for two reasons at once -- 32 further runs, and the corrected estimator -- and the run count is stated in the file so a reader can tell which is which.",
